Description: Resolve the per-test scratch file through $TMPDIR instead of hardcoding
             /var/tmp.  makeTempFileName() feeds the 7 io_tests cases that write a
             temporary LAS/LAZ file and read it straight back (extrabytes, issue44,
             can_encode_large_files, variable_chunks,
             compression_decompression_is_symmetric, writes_bbox_to_header,
             write_laz_with_no_points_and_read_back), all of which go through
             encode()/compare().  Measured: with /var/tmp made read-only
             (mount -t tmpfs -o ro,/var/tmp), the unpatched binary reports
             "21 ran / 14 PASSED / 7 FAILED", and the 7 named failures are exactly
             that set.
             On a system whose root filesystem is read-only, or which has no
             /var/tmp at all (HarmonyOS/OHOS, minimal containers), mkstemp() fails,
             its return value is ignored, and the later ofstream open silently
             produces nothing - the case then fails for reasons unrelated to
             lazperf.  $TMPDIR is the POSIX way to name the scratch directory; the
             current directory is the last resort because it is writable by
             definition.  With the patch the same read-only /var/tmp run reports
             21/21 PASSED.  Test count, test bodies and assertions are unchanged.
Origin: https://github.com/hobuinc/laz-perf/tree/3.4.0
Upstream: not submitted; general POSIX portability fix, upstreamable as-is
Source-Commit: c9f281490c8ee05391a7ed2a5e16fe0ef2083c7a
Modification-Layer: 1 (test harness scratch path only; no library source touched)
Knowledge-Ref: E002, DRAFT-lazperf-3.4.0-tests-hardcoded-var-tmp-readonly-rootfs, P005, P014

diff -ruN a/cpp/test/io_tests.cpp b/cpp/test/io_tests.cpp
--- a/cpp/test/io_tests.cpp
+++ b/cpp/test/io_tests.cpp
@@ -44,6 +44,10 @@
 #include <cstdio>
 #include "reader.hpp"
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#ifndef _WIN32
+#include <unistd.h>
+#endif

 namespace lazperf
 {
@@ -60,8 +64,24 @@
     GetTempPath(MAX_PATH, path);
     filename = std::string(path) + name;
 #else
-    std::string s("/var/tmp/fnXXXXXX");
-    mkstemp(const_cast<char *>(s.data()));
+    // Scratch files belong in $TMPDIR, which is what POSIX prescribes. A
+    // hardcoded /var/tmp makes every test that writes a temporary LAS/LAZ
+    // file fail on systems whose root filesystem is read-only or which have
+    // no /var/tmp at all (HarmonyOS/OHOS, minimal containers, ...): mkstemp
+    // fails, its return value is ignored, and the subsequent ofstream open
+    // silently yields nothing. Try $TMPDIR, then the current directory, which
+    // is writable by definition.
+    const char *tmpdir = std::getenv("TMPDIR");
+    std::string s = (tmpdir && *tmpdir ? std::string(tmpdir) : std::string(".")) +
+        "/lazperf-fnXXXXXX";
+    int fd = mkstemp(const_cast<char *>(s.data()));
+    if (fd < 0 && tmpdir && *tmpdir)
+    {
+        s = "./lazperf-fnXXXXXX";
+        fd = mkstemp(const_cast<char *>(s.data()));
+    }
+    if (fd >= 0)
+        ::close(fd);
     filename = s;
 #endif
     return filename;
